{#- One sign per lunch special of the week, for the board on the wall
    (client 2026-10-10: read from 6 to 14 feet). Shared by
    sign-day-specials.njk (colour) and sign-day-specials-bw.njk (`bw: true`).

    NO DAY OR DATE (client 2026-10-18): a sheet says "Today's Special", so
    it can be kept and put up again whenever that plate comes back with the
    same soup. The soup is on it, at the foot (client 2026-10-18: a soup
    sign of its own was tried the same day and archived while the board's
    layout is worked out), but the swap list says "the soup of the day"
    without naming it. A day's extraSides are "just for today", so they
    stay off. A plate repeated within the week with the same sides and soup
    is one page.

    Each plate is its own 11 × 17 portrait page, so the PDF prints the week
    as a stack and any one can be printed again on its own. The week is the
    newest one in specials.json, like the weekly post and the counter sign.

    SIZED FOR DISTANCE. About an inch of letter height reads at ten feet,
    so the plate is set at 1.4in and nothing on the sheet is under 0.4in.
    The sides ("A, B", or "Choice of side") go bare: "with" would only
    cost a line.

    THE SIDES BOX lists the Deli Salads (menu.json), which a customer can
    pick on a choice-of-side day and swap in for the set sides on any
    other (client 2026-10-10), so it says which of the two it is. -#}
{%- set plates = specials.days | latestWeek | distinctBy("special") %}
{%- set soupCat = (menu.categories | where("id", "soup"))[0] %}
{%- set sidesCat = (menu.categories | where("id", "sides"))[0] %}
{%- set deli = (sidesCat.items | selectattr("choices") | first) if sidesCat else null %}
<div class="ds-stack">
    {%- for d in plates %}
    {%- set sides = d | specialSides(true) %}
    <div class="canvas sign ds{% if bw %} sign--bw{% endif %}">
        <header class="ds-top">
            <p class="p-display ds-day ink-accent">Today&rsquo;s Special</p>
            <p class="ds-date ink-teal">Lunch special from 11am</p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-main">
            {#- A long name steps down a size, so it still fits in two lines;
                a third line pushes the soup box off the sheet. -#}
            <p class="p-display ds-special{% if d.special.length > 32 %} ds-special--longer{% elif d.special.length > 24 %} ds-special--long{% endif %} ink-teal">{{ d.special }}</p>
            {%- if sides %}
            <p class="ds-sides">{{ sides }}</p>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if specials.includesDrink %}
            <p class="ds-drink ink-accent">Includes a drink</p>
            {%- endif %}
        </div>

        {%- if deli %}
        <section class="ds-swap">
            <p class="p-label ds-box-label ink-accent">{% if d.anySide %}Pick your side{% else %}Swap a side for any of these{% endif %}</p>
            <ul class="ds-swap-list">
                {%- for c in deli.choices %}
                <li>{{ c }}</li>
                {%- endfor %}
                {%- if specials.soupSide %}
                <li>Cup of the soup of the day</li>
                {%- endif %}
            </ul>
        </section>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if d.soup %}
        <footer class="ds-soup">
            <p class="p-label ds-box-label ink-accent">Soup of the day</p>
            <div class="ds-soup-row">
                <p class="p-display ds-soup-name{% if d.soup.length > 22 %} ds-soup-name--long{% endif %} ink-teal">{{ d.soup }}</p>
                {%- if soupCat and soupCat.items %}
                <p class="ds-soup-price">{% for s in soupCat.items %}{% if not loop.first %} &middot; {% endif %}{{ s.name }} {{ s.price | money }}{% endfor %}</p>
                {%- endif %}
            </div>
        </footer>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
</div>
